---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Portrait from "../components/Portrait.astro";
import { experience, record, site } from "../data/site";
---

<Layout title="About Judge Cindy Allen" description="Cindy Allen is the Republican Justice of the Peace for Bastrop County Precinct 1, first elected in 2018 and seeking another term in 2026.">
  <section class="hero-wash relative overflow-hidden py-16 text-cream">
    <div class="star-field absolute inset-0"></div>
    <div class="relative mx-auto grid max-w-6xl items-center gap-10 px-4 md:grid-cols-[1.1fr_0.9fr] md:px-6">
      <div>
        <p class="font-mark text-[11px] text-gold">Biography · Record</p>
        <h1 class="font-display mt-3 text-5xl md:text-6xl">A Bastrop judge who already knows this docket.</h1>
        <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-lg text-cream/80">
          {site.honorific} is the sitting {site.office} in {site.county}. She took office January 1, 2019, and is asking Precinct 1 to keep her on the bench on November 3.
        </p>
      </div>
      <Portrait variant="about" class="max-w-md md:ml-auto" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 md:px-6">
    <div class="gold-rule mb-10"></div>
    <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed">
      When Cindy Allen first ran for this seat in 2018, she was a former municipal judge from Martindale in Caldwell County. She brought thirteen years in the Texas justice system with her: nine in juvenile justice, three in juvenile corrections, and one in adult probation.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted">
      Precinct 1 was an open seat that year, with Judge Donna Thomson leaving the bench. Allen won a four-person Republican primary runoff against former TABC executive director Sherry Cook, then defeated Democrat Dock Jackson in November with 56 percent of the vote. In 2022 she won a second term with 58 percent against Democrat Dayna Beck.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-relaxed">
      That is not a résumé assembled for a flyer. It is the path of someone who has already sat as a judge, already learned a county docket, and already been hired twice by the people who use this court.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-navy py-16 text-cream">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4 md:px-6">
      <p class="font-mark text-[11px] text-gold">Timeline</p>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-2 text-4xl">From first campaign to this ballot</h2>
      <ol class="mt-10 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-4">
        {
          record.map((item) => (
            <li class="border-t border-gold/40 pt-4">
              <p class="font-mark text-[11px] text-gold">{item.year}</p>
              <h3 class="font-display mt-2 text-2xl">{item.title}</h3>
              <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-cream/75">{item.detail}</p>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-16 md:px-6">
    <p class="font-mark text-[11px] text-red">What she brought to the bench</p>
    <h2 class="font-display mt-2 text-4xl">Experience before the title, and after it.</h2>
    <div class="mt-8 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-2">
      {
        experience.map((item) => (
          <article class="parchment rounded-sm border border-gold/30 p-6">
            <h3 class="font-display text-2xl">{item.title}</h3>
            <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-muted">{item.meta}</p>
            <p class="mt-3">{item.body}</p>
          </article>
        ))
      }
    </div>
    <p class="mt-10 max-w-3xl text-muted">
      Campaign facts on her 2018 and 2022 races are drawn from contemporaneous Austin American-Statesman election coverage and public election results. This page is political advertising, not a county biography.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>
